<xml xmlns="https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml"><block type="offer_generic" id="ai00081" x="50" y="50"><comment pinned="true" h="220" w="520">AI draft: When a member makes a Spend within 7 days before or after their birthday, they get the 'Complimentary Voucher Codes' privilege (ID 64). They can get it once per birthday, so once a year.&#10;&#10;Assumptions:&#10;- 'Within 7 days of their birthday' is read as 7 days before through 7 days after the birthday.&#10;- 'A spend' is read as the activity type SPEND (Spend), not PURCHASE (Shopping).&#10;- 'Complimentary voucher' is read as privilege 64 'Complimentary Voucher Codes', not 63 'COmplimentry'.&#10;- 'Once a year' comes from the occasion reward, which is given once per birthday. No other usage limit or frequency is set.&#10;- The birthday is taken from the member attribute date_of_birth for this draft.&#10;- Any spend amount counts, because no minimum was given.&#10;- No start or end date was given, so the offer runs indefinitely.&#10;&#10;Please confirm:&#10;- Two member attributes could hold the birthday: 'Date of Birth' (date_of_birth) and 'birthday date' (birthday_date). Which one should be used? The draft uses date_of_birth.</comment><statement name="activities"><block type="activity" id="ai00080"><statement name="ACTIVITY_CRITERIA"><block type="activity_criteria" id="ai00001"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" object="activity" attribute="h_bit_type" operators="in" payoperators="null" iscountertypevector="no" value="SPEND" visible_value="Spend" type="LOOKUP"></mutation><field name="OBJECT">activity</field><field name="attribute">h_bit_type</field><field name="operators">in</field></block></statement><statement name="RULES"><block type="rule" id="ai00019"><field name="IDENTIFIER">Window inside year</field><statement name="CONDITION"><block type="if_generic_adaptive" id="ai00006"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" object="member" attribute_level="MA_P" attribute="date_of_birth" op